---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import Walkthrough from '../components/Walkthrough.astro';
---

<Site title="Connect your AI to your apps">
  <main id="main" class="home-content">
    <header class="hero">
      <p class="release-pill">
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span> Open source <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> v0.1 alpha
      </p>
      <h1>Connect your AI to your apps.</h1>
      <p class="hero-description">
        Blindkit checks each request against your rules. API keys stay out of the AI’s code, and
        changes ask for your approval by default.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button" href="/docs/quickstart/">
          Get started <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
        <a class="secondary-button" href="#how-it-works">
          Try an example
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="hero-note">Runs on your computer. No Blindkit account needed.</p>
    </header>

    <section id="how-it-works" class="demo-section" aria-labelledby="example-title">
      <div class="demo-heading">
        <h2 id="example-title">Request preview</h2>
        <span>Choose an action to see what happens</span>
      </div>
      <Walkthrough />
    </section>

    <section class="benefits" aria-label="What Blindkit gives you">
      <div>
        <h2>Keys stay private.</h2>
        <p>Blindkit adds API keys when sending requests. Your AI never needs to handle them.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2>Permissions are explicit.</h2>
        <p>Let an action run, ask first, or block it. Changes need approval by default.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2>Requests are recorded.</h2>
        <p>Requests and results go into an activity log on your computer.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="setup" class="setup-section">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Start with one app</p>
        <h2>Run it locally.</h2>
        <p>
          The setup guide walks you through installing Blindkit and trying a sample API with your AI
          assistant.
        </p>
        <a class="button" href="/docs/quickstart/">
          Follow the setup guide <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <ol class="setup-steps">
        <li>
          <span aria-hidden="true">1</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Connect an app</h3>
            <p>Add its OpenAPI file—a list of the actions its API supports.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span aria-hidden="true">2</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Set your rules</h3>
            <p>Choose which actions can run and which need approval.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span aria-hidden="true">3</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Ask your AI</h3>
            <p>Use an AI app that supports MCP to find and run an action.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section id="questions" class="questions-section">
      <div>
        <h2>Before you connect.</h2>
        <p>
          Still exploring? <a href="/docs/">Start with the introduction.</a>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="questions-list">
        <details>
          <summary>Which apps can I connect?</summary>
          <p>
            Apps with an OpenAPI 3.0 JSON file describing their API. Some formats and sign-in
            methods are not supported yet. Check the <a href="/docs/config/">supported formats</a>{' '}
            before connecting an app.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Do I need a server or database?</summary>
          <p>
            No. Blindkit runs on your computer and saves settings and activity in local files. Setup
            needs Node 22 or 24, pnpm 10, and an AI app that supports MCP.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can my AI approve its own changes?</summary>
          <p>
            No. Your AI app must show you an approval form when one is required. If it cannot,
            Blindkit stops the request. Use an AI app you trust to show the form and report your
            answer.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Is it ready for important work?</summary>
          <p>
            This is an early release for trying things out. An independent security review and
            broader testing with AI apps are still needed. Start with the included example and read
            the <a href="/docs/security/">security guide</a> before connecting important data.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Site>
